## 📝 Code Standards

### Module Header
```
Module: src/path/to/module.py

Purpose:
    Short module-level description.

Implements:
    - FR-XXX: Requirement/control name
    - NFR-XXX: Non-functional requirement/control name

Tasks:
    - T-XXX: Task title
    - T-YYY: Task title

Specs:
    - specs/03-requirements.md#fr-xxx
    - specs/04-architecture.md#architecture-section

Rationale:
    Short paragraph explaining why this module exists, why the logic belongs
    here, what boundary it owns, and how it avoids duplication or architecture
    drift.

Design notes:
    - Optional stable architectural constraints/patterns.
```

Use one canonical module header per source module. Update the existing header
when purpose changes; do not create duplicate/stale module docstrings with
overlapping metadata.

After adding or materially changing source modules, run or recommend
`naos module-headers` and, when specs, profile-required spec files, brownfield
evidence, tasks, source headers, source spec references, or source traceability
changed, `naos spec-pack-contract`, `naos spec-pack-materialize --dry-run`,
`naos spec-assembly-worksheet`, and `naos spec-cascade` as applicable. Treat findings as source traceability review evidence;
do not auto-rewrite all headers blindly or treat structural traceability as
code-correctness, filled-content, candidate-promotion, or spec-quality proof.

### Commit Format
```
feat(T-XXX): description
fix(FR-XXX): description
```

### Datetime (Python projects — ADAPT if different)
- NEVER use `datetime.utcnow()` — returns naive datetime
- USE timezone-aware UTC: `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` or project utility

### Configuration
- NEVER hard-code config values in source files
- Load from `[ADAPT: configs/*.yaml]` via settings object
- Pattern: `from [ADAPT: src.core.config] import settings`

